Added `enqueueMany(items)` in `src/queue.js` next to the existing methods — it checks the total up front and throws `QueueFullError(capacity)` before touching the internal array, so an overflow leaves size, head, and contents untouched. Empty arrays short-circuit and return the current size. Added three tests covering success, overflow atomicity, and the empty no-op; `node --test` passes 31/31 and only those two files are modified.
